// Section 1 - Abstract
const abstractSection = [
  h1("1. Abstract"),
  p("This report presents a comprehensive study and technical documentation of an AI-powered voice-controlled home automation system utilizing USB relay modules. The proposed system integrates cutting-edge technologies including artificial intelligence, natural language processing (NLP), speech recognition, and Internet of Things (IoT) principles to create a hands-free, intelligent home control solution."),
  p("The system architecture leverages a microphone for capturing voice input, a speech-to-text engine (Whisper or Google STT), an AI processing unit for command interpretation, and USB relay modules to switch electrical appliances such as fans, lights, and other household devices. The project demonstrates an interdisciplinary approach involving Computer Science, Electronics and Communication Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, and Civil Engineering."),
  p("Key outcomes include: successful hands-free control of multiple appliances, real-time AI command interpretation, cost-effective implementation using commercially available components, and a scalable framework that can be expanded to support smart home ecosystems. Future enhancements include IoT platform integration, mobile app control, and full autonomous operation using environmental sensor data."),
  space(1),
  pageBreak()
];

// Section 2 - Introduction
const introSection = [
  h1("2. Introduction"),
  h2("2.1 Background"),
  p("The concept of home automation has evolved significantly over the past two decades. Traditional systems required manual switching of physical controls, which limited accessibility, especially for elderly individuals or persons with disabilities. The emergence of the Internet of Things (IoT), artificial intelligence, and advanced speech processing has opened new avenues for intuitive, hands-free home control systems."),
  p("Voice-controlled systems, popularized by commercial products such as Amazon Alexa, Google Home, and Apple's Siri, have demonstrated the viability and consumer acceptance of voice-based interfaces. However, these commercial solutions often involve cloud dependency, subscription fees, and privacy risks. The project presented in this report proposes a localized, open-source-inspired alternative that brings similar capabilities at significantly lower cost, with greater customizability."),
  h2("2.2 Motivation"),
  p("The growing demand for smart homes and assistive technology for disabled individuals motivated this project. The team identified a gap between high-end commercial systems and accessible, affordable alternatives. USB relay modules, which are inexpensive and widely available, offer a practical bridge between software AI and physical electrical control — without requiring complete home rewiring or proprietary hardware."),
  h2("2.3 Scope of the Report"),
  p("This report covers all aspects of the project lifecycle from initial concept and system design to implementation, testing, and future roadmap. It documents the hardware components, software stack, AI pipeline, circuit diagrams, engineering collaboration, and performance analysis. The report serves both as a technical reference and as a proposal for future development."),
  space(1),
  pageBreak()
];

