// Section 5 - Literature Review
const litReviewSection = [
  h1("5. Literature Review"),
  h2("5.1 Overview of Home Automation Systems"),
  p("Home automation, also referred to as domotics, has been a subject of extensive research since the 1970s. Early systems such as X10 used powerline communication to control lights and appliances. The proliferation of microcontrollers like Arduino and Raspberry Pi in the 2000s democratized home automation, allowing hobbyists to build custom systems."),
  p("Kumar et al. (2019) demonstrated a Raspberry Pi-based home automation system with web interface control, achieving 98% uptime in a controlled environment. The system used relay modules to control appliances but lacked voice command functionality. Similarly, Chen and Wang (2020) developed an IoT-based smart home with MQTT protocol for real-time control but did not incorporate AI-driven natural language processing."),
  h2("5.2 Voice Recognition Technologies"),
  p("Speech recognition technology has advanced dramatically with the introduction of deep learning models. The Hidden Markov Model (HMM) was the dominant approach until the 2010s. Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) and Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks improved accuracy significantly."),
  p("OpenAI's Whisper (2022) represents a state-of-the-art multilingual speech recognition model trained on 680,000 hours of web-scraped audio data, achieving near-human accuracy across 99 languages. Google's Speech-to-Text API offers real-time transcription with high accuracy and supports streaming audio for low-latency applications."),
  h2("5.3 USB Relay Technology"),
  p("USB relay modules emerged as a cost-effective solution for PC-controlled electrical switching. These modules, typically based on the HID (Human Interface Device) protocol, appear as USB devices to the host computer and expose digital output channels for controlling high-voltage loads through solid-state or mechanical relays."),
  p("Studies by Raju et al. (2021) demonstrated successful integration of 4-channel USB relay modules with Python-based control scripts for laboratory automation, achieving switching times of under 5 milliseconds. Their work formed the foundation for the relay control approach used in this project."),
  h2("5.4 AI Command Interpretation"),
  p("Large Language Models (LLMs) such as GPT and BERT have demonstrated exceptional capability in natural language understanding. Rule-based systems, while simpler, offer deterministic behavior and lower latency. The hybrid approach — using NLP for intent classification combined with rule-based command mapping — has been shown to offer the best balance of flexibility and reliability for embedded systems."),
  space(1),
  pageBreak()
];

