// Section 8 - Working Principle
const workingSection = [
  h1("8. Working Principle"),
  h2("8.1 Step-by-Step Process"),
  p("The system operates through a continuous listen-process-act loop. Below is the detailed working principle of each stage:"),
  space(1),
  h3("Step 1: Voice Input Capture"),
  p("The user speaks a command such as 'Turn on the fan' or 'Switch off the bedroom light.' The microphone captures the acoustic sound waves and the ADC converts them to a Pulse Code Modulated (PCM) digital audio stream, typically at 16kHz, 16-bit, mono format for optimal speech recognition performance."),
  h3("Step 2: Speech-to-Text Conversion"),
  p("The digital audio stream is passed to the Speech-to-Text (STT) engine. Whisper, developed by OpenAI, uses an encoder-decoder transformer architecture trained on 680,000 hours of labeled audio. The encoder processes the mel spectrogram of the audio while the decoder autoregressively generates the text transcription with high accuracy."),
  h3("Step 3: AI Command Interpretation"),
  p("The text transcript is processed by the NLP/AI engine. The engine performs: (a) tokenization of the input text, (b) intent classification (turn on, turn off, dim, query status), (c) entity extraction (which appliance — fan, light, AC), and (d) optional context handling (bedroom light vs. living room light)."),
  h3("Step 4: Command Mapping"),
  p("The extracted intent and entity are mapped to a specific relay channel and state using a configuration dictionary. For example: {'fan': {'channel': 1, 'on': HIGH, 'off': LOW}, 'light': {'channel': 2, 'on': HIGH, 'off': LOW}}. This mapping is fully customizable for any appliance configuration."),
  h3("Step 5: Relay Triggering"),
  p("A Python script sends the HID command to the USB relay module using the pyusb or hid library. The relay module receives the command and energizes or de-energizes the corresponding relay coil, physically opening or closing the high-voltage circuit to the appliance."),
  h3("Step 6: Appliance State Change"),
  p("The connected appliance (fan, light, etc.) responds to the relay state change — turning on or off as commanded. An optional feedback mechanism (text-to-speech or LED indicator) confirms the action to the user."),
  space(1),
  h2("8.2 Timing Analysis"),
  makeTable(
    ["Stage", "Local Processing", "Cloud STT Processing"],
    [
      ["Voice capture (1-3 sec utterance)", "1,000-3,000 ms", "1,000-3,000 ms"],
      ["Speech-to-Text conversion", "100-300 ms", "500-2000 ms"],
      ["AI interpretation", "50-100 ms", "50-100 ms"],
      ["Command mapping", "< 5 ms", "< 5 ms"],
      ["Relay actuation", "< 5 ms", "< 5 ms"],
      ["Total response latency", "~200-500 ms", "~600-2500 ms"],
    ],
    [3500, 3000, 2860]
  ),
  space(1),
  pageBreak()
];

