// Section 15 - Disadvantages
const disadvantagesSection = [
  h1("15. Disadvantages and Limitations"),
  h2("15.1 Technical Limitations"),
  p("Despite its advantages, the system has several limitations that must be acknowledged:"),
  bullet("Microphone quality dependency: Performance degrades significantly in noisy environments. Background TV noise, air conditioning sound, or multiple people speaking simultaneously can cause misinterpretation."),
  bullet("AI misinterpretation risk: Even state-of-the-art STT systems can mishear commands. For example, 'Turn off the fan' might be misheard as 'Turn on the fan' in noisy conditions, with potentially undesired results."),
  bullet("Continuous power requirement: The control computer (Raspberry Pi or PC) must remain powered at all times, consuming 5-15W continuously. This adds to the electricity bill."),
  bullet("Initial setup complexity: Configuring the system, especially the relay-to-appliance mapping and NLP customization, requires technical knowledge and is not trivial for non-technical users."),
  bullet("Privacy in cloud mode: If using cloud-based STT (Google STT, Azure), voice data is transmitted to remote servers, raising privacy concerns."),
  bullet("Relay channel limitation: USB relay modules typically support 4-8 channels, limiting the number of independently controllable appliances without additional modules."),
  bullet("Latency in cloud mode: Cloud-based STT can introduce 0.5-2 seconds of latency, which may feel sluggish to users."),
  space(1),
  h2("15.2 Safety Considerations"),
  p("The system handles high-voltage AC circuits through relay switching. Incorrect wiring or component failure could create electrical hazards. All installations must be performed by qualified electricians, and the system must comply with local electrical codes and regulations."),
  h2("15.3 Mitigation Strategies"),
  p("Many limitations can be mitigated through careful design choices: directional microphones reduce noise pickup, hardware confirmation buttons provide manual override, fuses and circuit breakers protect against relay failures, and user training improves voice command success rates."),
  space(1),
  pageBreak()
